El problema más probable es que si el usuario sale de la sesión manualmente (presionando "Inicio" o "Perfiles") antes de que se cumpla el tiempo límite, el historial se perdía porque la aplicación solo guardaba al completar el tiempo.

He modificado `App.tsx` para asegurar que **cualquier progreso se guarde automáticamente** antes de salir de la pantalla de juego, ya sea por tiempo cumplido o por salir manualmente.

# Updated files:

## App.tsx

Added `saveSessionData` helper function and integrated it into `handleReturnToSelection` and `handleGoHome`. This ensures that session history is persisted even if the user exits the activity early, solving the issue of missing session logs.

```typescript
// ... existing code ...
  const saveSessionData = () => {
    if (!currentUserProfile || !sessionStartTime || currentSessionHistory.length === 0) return;

    const sessionRecord: SessionRecord = {
        startTime: sessionStartTime,
        endTime: new Date().toISOString(),
        activities: currentSessionHistory,
    };

    const updatedProfile = {
        ...currentUserProfile,
        history: [...(currentUserProfile.history || []), sessionRecord],
    };

    updateProfile(updatedProfile);
  };

  const handleReturnToSelection = () => {
    saveSessionData(); // Guardar antes de salir
    setCurrentUserProfile(null);
    setCurrentActivity(null);
    setGameState(GameState.PROFILE_SELECTION);
  }

  const handleGoHome = () => {
    saveSessionData(); // Guardar antes de salir
    setCurrentUserProfile(null);
    setCurrentActivity(null);
    setGameState(GameState.WELCOME);
  };
// ... existing code ...

The "unexpected error" likely occurred because the `BadgeNotification.tsx` component was imported in `App.tsx` but the file itself was not successfully created in the file system. I will create this missing file and also refine `App.tsx` to ensure the transition animations don't reset the game state (like star streaks) unnecessarily.

